1
00:00:00,655 --> 00:00:02,850
你大概听说过“朝九晚五”，
You've probably heard of 9 to 5,

2
00:00:02,955 --> 00:00:05,125
但你听说过“996”吗？
but what about 996?

3
00:00:05,125 --> 00:00:07,345
每天实行“996”，
Working 996 every day

4
00:00:07,345 --> 00:00:12,015
就会让你多加班二三十个小时。
makes your overtime longer than 20 or 30 hours.

5
00:00:12,015 --> 00:00:13,890
这肯定会伤害身体。
It surely harms your body.

6
00:00:13,965 --> 00:00:17,285
这已成为人们对“996”的普遍感受。
That's become a popular sentiment towards 996,

7
00:00:17,285 --> 00:00:20,815
所谓“996”，就是每天从早九点工作到晚九点，
the culture of working from 9 a.m. to 9 p.m.

8
00:00:20,815 --> 00:00:22,310
每周工作六天。
six days a week.

9
00:00:22,635 --> 00:00:23,885
这种工作制正变得越来越普遍，
It's become more common

10
00:00:23,885 --> 00:00:26,510
尤其是在中国竞争激烈的科技行业，
in China's super competitive tech industry

11
00:00:26,875 --> 00:00:30,580
并引发了全国对工作与生活平衡的讨论，
and has sparked a nationwide debate about work-life balance,

12
00:00:30,695 --> 00:00:33,140
其中许多讨论发生在社交媒体上。
much of it playing out on social media.

13
00:00:33,275 --> 00:00:35,555
上个月，一场抵制运动兴起，
Last month, a movement of dissent took off

14
00:00:35,555 --> 00:00:38,460
地点是微软旗下的代码共享平台GitHub。
on Microsoft's code sharing platform, GitHub.

15
00:00:39,085 --> 00:00:41,925
这场运动被称为“996.ICU”，
It's dubbed 996 ICU,

16
00:00:41,925 --> 00:00:44,705
意指实行“996”工作制，
implying that working 996 will land you

17
00:00:44,705 --> 00:00:46,490
最终可能让你住进重症监护室。
in the intensive care unit.

18
00:00:46,645 --> 00:00:49,515
“被996困住的年轻人”这一话题标签，
The hashtag young people trapped by 996

19
00:00:49,515 --> 00:00:52,160
也在中国社交媒体上广泛传播。
has also made the rounds on Chinese social media.

20
00:00:52,365 --> 00:00:54,905
人们借此分享高压工作的经历，
It's a way to share stressful work experiences

21
00:00:54,905 --> 00:00:58,280
并点名批评实行这种严苛工作制的公司。
and call out companies that implement the grueling schedule.

22
00:00:58,935 --> 00:01:01,055
“对于一些初创企业和大公司，
"For some startups and big companies,

23
00:01:01,055 --> 00:01:03,295
它们需要通过工作来与其他企业竞争，
they need their work to compete with other firms

24
00:01:03,295 --> 00:01:05,920
而员工正是这种竞争力的核心。”
and employees are at the core of that competitiveness."

25
00:01:06,735 --> 00:01:10,265
“偶尔为事业拼搏一下是可以接受的，
"It is acceptable to struggle for your career once in a while,

26
00:01:10,265 --> 00:01:11,625
但不要让它成为常态。
but don't make it a norm.

27
00:01:11,625 --> 00:01:14,405
我认为最好的办法是提高效率。”
I think the best way is to increase efficiency."

28
00:01:14,405 --> 00:01:16,835
中国一些大型公司的负责人，
The heads of some of China's biggest companies

29
00:01:16,835 --> 00:01:18,410
也加入了这场讨论。
have also joined the debate.

30
00:01:19,085 --> 00:01:21,640
阿里巴巴的马云在微博上发文表示：
Alibaba's Jack Ma posting on Weibo,

31
00:01:21,855 --> 00:01:24,875
“我个人认为，能够实行996，
"I personally think that being able to work 996

32
00:01:24,875 --> 00:01:26,230
是一种巨大的福气。
is a huge blessing.

33
00:01:26,385 --> 00:01:28,925
如果你不比别人付出更多时间和精力，
If you don't put out more time and energy than others,

34
00:01:28,925 --> 00:01:31,140
又怎么能获得你想要的成功？”
how can you achieve the success you want?"

35
00:01:31,825 --> 00:01:33,485
马云后来澄清说，
Ma later clarified, saying

36
00:01:33,485 --> 00:01:36,520
他并不赞成强制实行“996”，
he didn't condone mandatory 996 schedules,

37
00:01:36,725 --> 00:01:38,235
而只是想赞扬那些，
but just wanted to praise those

38
00:01:38,235 --> 00:01:40,715
自愿投入这些工作时间的人。
who put in the hours voluntarily.

39
00:01:40,715 --> 00:01:45,190
电商巨头京东的首席执行官兼联合创始人刘强东，
Richard Liu, CEO and co-founder of e-commerce giant JD.com,

40
00:01:45,395 --> 00:01:48,345
则在微博上说得更直接：
put it more bluntly in his Weibo post, saying,

41
00:01:48,345 --> 00:01:50,710
“混日子的人不是我的兄弟。”
"Slackers are not my brothers."

42
00:01:51,185 --> 00:01:53,610
“996”并非中国独有。
996 is not unique to China.

43
00:01:54,355 --> 00:01:57,145
SpaceX的首席执行官兼创始人埃隆·马斯克，
Elon Musk, CEO and founder of SpaceX,

44
00:01:57,145 --> 00:02:01,365
在推特上说，他经常每周工作120小时。
said on Twitter he often clocks 120 hours a week.

45
00:02:01,365 --> 00:02:04,880
他说，从来没有人靠每周工作40小时改变世界。
Nobody, he said, ever changed the world on 40.

46
00:02:05,105 --> 00:02:07,975
但自愿长时间工作与被迫加班，
But choosing to work long hours or being forced

47
00:02:07,975 --> 00:02:09,740
完全是两回事。
are two issues entirely.

48
00:02:09,885 --> 00:02:13,180
一位中国律师表示，这其中存在法律红线。
One Chinese attorney says there is a legal red line.

49
00:02:13,305 --> 00:02:16,985
根据中国劳动法，
According to Chinese labor law,

50
00:02:16,985 --> 00:02:19,525
大多数员工适用标准工时制度，
most employees are subject to standard working time,

51
00:02:19,525 --> 00:02:21,770
即每天工作不超过八小时，
which is no more than eight hours per day,

52
00:02:21,805 --> 00:02:23,450
每周不超过40小时，
no more than 40 hours per week,

53
00:02:23,625 --> 00:02:25,215
且每周至少休息一天。
and at least one day off every week.

54
00:02:25,215 --> 00:02:28,035
所以，“996”工作制违反了法律，
So the 996 working time violates the law

55
00:02:28,035 --> 00:02:30,930
其每日和每周工作时间均超出了规定。
in terms of both working time every day and every week.

56
00:02:32,285 --> 00:02:35,695
“对于年轻人来说，多年以后，
"For young people, after many years,

57
00:02:35,695 --> 00:02:38,725
他们或许会觉得自己曾有一份宝贵的工作机会，
they may think they had a valuable work opportunity,

58
00:02:38,725 --> 00:02:42,205
但也可能后悔自己被廉价地出卖了。”
but they may also regret they had sold themselves cheaply."

59
00:02:42,205 --> 00:02:45,470
有人认为，这样的代价并不值得。
A cost that some say just isn't worth it.

60
00:02:45,845 --> 00:02:47,764
CGTN记者Frances Kuo报道。
Frances Kuo, CGTN.

